  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of the Ghana Agroforestry Technical Working Group (ATWG)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports the establishment and first-year operations of the Ghana&#xa0; Agroforestry Technical Working Group (ATWG), a national, multi-stakeholder platform dedicated to integrating agroforestry into sustainable agricultural production and land-use policy. Building on a year-long participatory process facilitated by i4Policy with support from the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and the Netherlands Embassy in Ghana, the ATWG will bring together government agencies, cooperatives, private sector , NGOs, development partners, and research institutions.&#xa0;The group will validate and finalise the Agroforestry Policy Insights and Action Framework, with a specific focus on agroforestry systems as a pathway to an agricultural sector more equipped to handle climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
